<%- include('partials/header’) %>
    <main class="content-area">
        <div class="care-section">
            <h2>Essential Cat Care Guide</h2>

            <div class="care-topic">
                <h3>Nutrition and Feeding</h3>
                <p>Proper nutrition is essential for your cat's health. Cats are obligate carnivores and require specific nutrients that come from meat.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Feed high-quality cat food appropriate for their age and health status</li>
                    <li>Provide fresh, clean water daily in multiple locations</li>
                    <li>Monitor portion sizes to maintain healthy weight</li>
                    <li>Consider wet food for additional moisture intake</li>
                    <li>Never feed dog food or human food without veterinary approval</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="care-topic">
                <h3>Litter Box Care</h3>
                <p>Proper litter box maintenance is crucial for your cat's well-being and house training success.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Scoop litter box daily</li>
                    <li>Complete litter change weekly</li>
                    <li>Provide one box per cat, plus one extra</li>
                    <li>Place boxes in quiet, accessible locations</li>
                    <li>Use unscented, clumping litter unless cat shows other preferences</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="care-topic">
                <h3>Health and Veterinary Care</h3>
                <p>Regular veterinary care helps prevent health issues and ensures a long, healthy life.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Annual check-ups and vaccinations</li>
                    <li>Regular parasite prevention</li>
                    <li>Dental care and cleaning when recommended</li>
                    <li>Spaying or neutering</li>
                    <li>Watch for changes in behavior, appetite, or litter box habits</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="care-topic">
                <h3>Grooming</h3>
                <p>While cats are generally good self-groomers, they still need some grooming assistance.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Brush regularly to prevent matting and hairballs</li>
                    <li>Trim nails every few weeks</li>
                    <li>Check and clean ears if needed</li>
                    <li>Brush teeth or provide dental treats</li>
                    <li>Professional grooming for long-haired cats if needed</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="care-topic">
                <h3>Environmental Enrichment</h3>
                <p>Cats need mental and physical stimulation to stay happy and healthy.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Provide scratching posts and climbing areas</li>
                    <li>Rotate toys to maintain interest</li>
                    <li>Create window viewing areas</li>
                    <li>Include interactive play sessions daily</li>
                    <li>Consider cat trees and hiding spots for security</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="care-topic">
                <h3>Indoor Safety</h3>
                <p>Creating a safe indoor environment is crucial for your cat's well-being.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Secure windows and balconies</li>
                    <li>Keep toxic plants and substances out of reach</li>
                    <li>Store cleaning supplies safely</li>
                    <li>Provide multiple resting spots at different heights</li>
                    <li>Keep small objects that could be swallowed secured</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <p class="source-credit">
                Content sourced from <a href="https://www.aspca.org/pet-care/cat-care/general-cat-care">aspca</a>.
                For specific medical advice, please consult with your veterinarian.
            </p>
        </div>
    </main>


